WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.720
&gt;&gt; GOOD AFTERNOON.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.560
I AM BETSY HUMPHREYS, DEPUTY

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:15.809
DIRECTOR OF THE NATIONAL LIBRARY

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:18.360
OF MEDICINE, AND ON BEHALF OF

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.360
THE FABULOUS MULTIDISCIPLINARY

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.360
STAFF OF THE NATIONAL LIBRARY OF

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.360
MEDICINE AND THE FRIENDS OF THE

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.360
NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE,

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.360
WELCOME TO ALL OF YOU.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.539
WE ARE REALLY -- THOSE OF YOU

00:00:25.539 --> 00:00:27.260
WHO ARE IN THE ROOM AND WE THINK

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.409
WE HAVE A LOT OF PEOPLE WATCHING

00:00:28.409 --> 00:00:30.240
US, THE VIDEOCAST ACROSS THE

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.519
COUNTRY, MAYBE AROUND THE WORLD

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:33.090
AS WELL.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.790
SO WE ARE DELIGHTED, HOWEVER,

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.810
THAT SO MANY DISTINGUISHED

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:39.320
GUESTS HAVE TRAVELED HERE TO BE

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.470
WITH US, SOME OVER LONG

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:44.140
DISTANCES, AND I WOULD LIKE TO

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.290
EXTEND OUR SPECIAL WELCOME TO

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:50.030
LOIS FLATLEY AND A NUMBER OF

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:52.650
PATTI'S SISTERS, BROTHERS AND

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.040
OTHER RELATIVES WHO WERE ABLE TO

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.930
COME WITH US, WE'RE PARTICULARLY

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.010
DELIGHTED TO HAVE THEM HERE.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.730
I THINK THAT NLM IS VERY RICH IN

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.690
ITS ADVISORS, PARTNERS AND U.S.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.540
SUPPORTERS AND I'M GOING TO

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.810
ACKNOWLEDGE A FEW OF THEM, I

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.920
CAN'T POSSIBLY ACKNOWLEDGE YOU,

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.880
BUT FIRST BOB GRENNIS, CHAIR OF

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:14.930
THE NLM BOARD OF REJEPTS, WE

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.190
HAVE A NUMBER OF OTHER REGENTS,

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.900
BOTH PRESENT AND FORMER, WITH US

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.970
TODAY, WHICH IS GREAT.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.270
WE HAVE BARBARA REDMOND,

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:25.310
PRESIDENT, AND GLEN CAMPBELL,

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:26.582
CHAIR OF THE BOARD OF THE

00:01:26.582 --> 00:01:28.530
FRIENDS OF NLM AND A NUMBER OF

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.260
OTHER FRIENDS' FRIENDS IN THE

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.130
ROOM.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:39.450
WE HAVE TERESA NAHH, KEVIN

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.049
BALOZIAN, EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR OF

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:43.140
THE MEDICAL LIBRARY ASSOCIATION

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.390
AND A NUMBER OF OTHER LEADERS

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.479
AND SUPPORTERS INCLUDING

00:01:47.479 --> 00:01:49.700
INTERNATIONAL LIBRARY OF

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.770
MEDICINE, AND I BELIEVE WE HAVE

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.869
DOUG PRISMA, PRESIDENT AND CEO

00:01:54.869 --> 00:01:56.460
OF THE AMERICAN MEDICAL

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.170
INFORMATICS ASSOCIATION.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.970
NLM HAS NOT ONLY MANY PARTNERS

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.510
AROUND THE WORLD AND OUT IN THE

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:03.820
FIELD, BUT WE HAVE A LOT OF

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:05.409
GREAT PARTNERS ACROSS FEDERAL

00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:06.840
AGENCIES AND OF COURSE HERE

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.860
WITHIN THE NIH, AND WE ARE VERY

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:13.569
GLAD THAT I THINK SUZANNA FOX,

00:02:13.569 --> 00:02:16.370
WHO IS THE CHIEF TECHNOLOGY

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.459
OFFICER OF THE HHS IS HERE, AND

00:02:18.459 --> 00:02:22.000
I THINK PERHAPS ALSO WE HAVE

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.520
JOHN WHITE, WHO IS THE DEPUTY

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.470
NATIONAL COORDINATOR OF THE

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:27.510
NATIONAL -- DEPUTY NATIONAL

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:28.510
COORDINATOR OF HEALTH

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.320
INFORMATION KEK NOLG AND FROM

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.860
RIGHT HERE AT NIH, GARY GIBBONS,

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:36.320
WHO IS THE DIRECTOR OF NHLBI AND

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.489
PAT GRADY, WHO IS THE DIRECTOR

00:02:37.489 --> 00:02:38.700
OF THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.390
NURSING RESEARCH, AND I HAVE TO

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.370
SAY WITHIN HERE WE REALLY

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:45.110
WELCOME THE VERY LARGE NUMBER OF

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:46.480
NURSING LEADERS FROM ACROSS THE

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.960
COUNTRY WHO ARE WITH US TODAY.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:52.430
THANK YOU ALL FOR BEING HERE.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.870
AND WE HAVE FRANCIS COLLINS.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:55.870
[LAUGHTER]

00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:01.050
THE DIRECTOR OF NIH.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:05.480
[APPLAUSE]

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:08.610
SO TODAY IS DEFINITELY A DAY FOR

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.400
LOOKING TO THE FUTURE, BUT I'M

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.630
GOING TO TAKE A FEW MINUTES TO

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.360
SET THE STAGE BY REVIEWING SOME

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.510
HISTORICAL MILESTONES THAT HAVE

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:16.970
BROUGHT NLM TO ITS CURRENT

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:18.780
POSITION WITHIN THE WORLD OF

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:19.810
BIOMEDICAL AND HEALTH

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:21.459
INFORMATION AND DATA.

00:03:21.459 --> 00:03:26.470
AS IT HAPPENS, 2016 IS THE 180TH

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.060
ANNIVERSARY OF THE ESTABLISHMENT

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.910
OF NLM'S EARLIEST PREDECESSOR

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.150
LIBRARY WITHIN THE OFFICE OF THE

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.670
SURGEON GENERAL OF THE ARMY.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:39.300
AND 2016 IS ALSO THE 60TH

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.959
ANNIVERSARY OF THE PASSAGE OF

00:03:41.959 --> 00:03:43.180
THE NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:47.550
ACT, WHICH IN 1956 TRANSFERRED

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.239
THE ARMED FORCES MEDICAL LIBRARY

00:03:49.239 --> 00:03:51.129
FROM THE DEPARTMENT OF DEFENSE

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:52.739
INTO WHAT WAS THEN THE

00:03:52.739 --> 00:03:54.550
DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH EDUCATION

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:57.790
AND WELFARE, AND IN ADDITION TO

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:01.159
RENAMING THE LIBRARY, THIS ACT,

00:04:01.159 --> 00:04:02.379
WHICH WAS CO-SPONSORED BY

00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:03.811
SENATORS LISTER HILL, YOU'RE

00:04:03.811 --> 00:04:05.940
HERE TODAY, AND JOHN F. KENNEDY,

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:08.599
GAVE NLM ITS GREAT MISSION, AND

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:10.360
I'M GOING TO READ THIS TO YOU.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:12.920
QUOTE, TO ASSIST THE ADVANCEMENT

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.270
OF THE MEDICAL AND RELATED

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:16.980
SCIENCES AND TO AID THE

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.250
DISSEMINATION AND EXCHANGE OF

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.699
SCIENTIFIC AND OTHER INFORMATION

00:04:21.699 --> 00:04:23.440
IMPORTANT TO THE PROGRESS OF

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:24.950
MEDICINE AND TO THE PUBLIC

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:27.280
HEALTH."

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.430
LET ME HASTEN TO ADD FOR THIS

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:31.880
AUDIENCE THAT THE ACT EXPLICITLY

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.500
DEFINED MEDICINE AND MEDICAL TO

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.900
INCLUDE PREVENTIVE AND

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.460
THERAPEUTIC MEDICINE, DENTISTRY,

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.960
PHARMACY, HOSPITALIZATION,

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.740
NURSING, PUBLIC HEALTH, AND THE

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.910
FUNDAMENTAL SCIENCES RELATED

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.630
THERETO, AND OTHER RELATED

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:49.180
FIELDS OF STUDY, RESEARCH OR

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.960
ACTIVITY.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.060
IN ADDITION TO ENUMERATING THE

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.590
BASIC NLM FUNCTIONS THAT SUPPORT

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:57.360
PERMANENT ACCESS TO THE

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.130
BIOMEDICAL LITERATURE, THE LAW

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.090
ALSO REQUIRES THE LIBRARY,

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:02.900
QUOTE, TO ENGAGE IN SUCH OTHER

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.440
ACTIVITIES AS THE SECRETARY

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.380
DETERMINES APPROPRIATE.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:10.280
SO IN THE 1960s, THE SCOPE OF

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.110
NLM WAS RADICALLY EXPANDED BY

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:15.540
BOTH THE CONGRESS AND THE

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:19.720
SECRETARY IN TERMS OF ADDING

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.240
GRANT AUTHORITY, CREATING OUR

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.860
FIRST INTRAMURAL RESEARCH

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:25.210
DIVISION, THE LISTER HILL

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:27.370
NATIONAL CENTER FOR BIOMEDICAL

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.880
COMMUNICATION, SPECIFICALLY IN

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:30.650
JOINING US TO CREATE A

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:34.340
TOXICOLOGY INFORMATION PROGRAM,

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.121
TRANSFERRING THE PUBLIC HEALTH

00:05:36.121 --> 00:05:40.090
SERVICE AUDIOVISUAL FACILITY TO

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:41.440
THE NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.060
FROM THE CDC, AND I COULD GO ON.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:49.430
THE SCOPE OF WHAT WE DO AND

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:52.711
PARTICULARLY THE ADDITION OF OUR

00:05:52.711 --> 00:05:56.240
GRANT PROGRAM IN 1965 AND THE

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:57.729
REQUIREMENT TO CREATE THE

00:05:57.729 --> 00:05:59.250
NATIONAL NETWORK OF LIBRARIES OF

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:00.960
MEDICINE JUST RADICALLY EXPANDED

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.070
WHAT THE LIBRARY DID, AND SET

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.639
THE STAGE, THE PROGRAMS THAT

00:06:05.639 --> 00:06:07.259
CAME OUT OF THOSE EXPANSIONS SET

00:06:07.259 --> 00:06:09.539
THE STAGE FOR THE NEXT BIG SET

00:06:09.539 --> 00:06:11.940
OF EXPANSIONS WHICH BEGAN IN

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:16.110
1988 WITH THE LEGISLATION THAT

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:17.259
CREATED THE NATIONAL CENTER FOR

00:06:17.259 --> 00:06:19.229
BIOTECHNOLOGY INFORMATION WITHIN

00:06:19.229 --> 00:06:23.810
NLM ACTS, WHICH ALSO EXPANDED

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:24.930
OUR ACTIVITIES IN HEALTH

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:28.400
SERVICES RESEARCH, GENERAL

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:29.810
ASSIGNMENTS TO THE GOVERNMENT

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:32.400
BUT ALSO TO NLM IN TERMS OF

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.100
CLINICAL TRIALS REGISTRATION AND

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.030
TO THE NIH IN TERMS OF PUBLIC

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:38.870
ACCESS.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:40.919
I THINK THAT I ALWAYS SAY THAT

00:06:40.919 --> 00:06:43.080
FEBRUARY 2000 WAS ONE OF THE

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:44.580
GREAT MONTHS IN THE HISTORY OF

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:46.389
NLM BECAUSE IT WAS THE MONTH

00:06:46.389 --> 00:06:48.550
THAT BOTH PUBMED CENTRAL, OUR

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:51.750
PUBLIC ACCESS TO -- OUR PUBLIC

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.060
ARCHIVE OF ARTICLES IN

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.139
BIOMEDICINE, BUT ALSO

00:06:56.139 --> 00:06:57.800
CLINICALTRIALS.GOV DEBUTED THAT

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.380
SAME MONTH.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:02.730
SO I THINK THAT WE LATER WERE

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.220
ASSIGNED RESPONSIBILITIES BY

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:06.780
SECRETARIES IN AREAS RELATED TO

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.490
HEALTH DATA STANDARDS AND HEALTH

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:11.370
SERVICES RESEARCH, AND WE HAVE

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:14.500
ARRIVED TODAY WITH A VERY WIDE

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:17.020
RANGING SET OF ACTIVITIES THAT

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:21.130
AFFECT VIRTUALLY ALL ASPECTS OF

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:22.410
BIOMEDICAL INFORMATION AND

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:24.900
HEALTH DATA IN SOME WAY, SHAPE

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:28.460
OR FORM, AND PATTI COMES TO US

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:31.520
NOW AS THE 19TH PERSON, THE

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:33.289
FIRST NURSE AND THE FIRST WOMAN

00:07:33.289 --> 00:07:35.990
TO OFFICIALLY BE APPOINTED AS

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:38.020
THE LIBRARY'S DIRECTOR.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.759
THE FIRST APPOINTED DIRECTOR WAS

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:41.880
ACTUALLY JOHN SHAW BILLING,

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.470
BEFORE THAT, THERE WASN'T A

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:45.470
DIRECTOR.

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:47.340
HE WAS APPOINTED IN 1865, AND AS

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:50.680
MANY OF YOU KNOW, HE WAS THEN

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.880
ACTUALLY PURPOSELY TRANSFORMED

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.280
THE LIBRARY OF THE SURGEON

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:55.510
GENERAL'S OFFICE INTO A NATIONAL

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:56.590
MEDICAL LIBRARY.

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:58.539
HE ESTABLISHED THE INDEX MEDICUS

00:07:58.539 --> 00:08:00.180
AND OTHER CATALOGING INDEXING

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:02.020
THINGS THAT ARE A PRECURSOR OF

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:03.509
PUBMED TODAY.

00:08:03.509 --> 00:08:09.640
HE WAS ALSO INVOLVED IN GREATLY

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:12.440
EXPANDING THE COLLECTION SO WHEN

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:13.660
HE LEFT, WE WERE THE LARGEST

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:14.900
MEDICAL LIBRARY IN THE WORLD, AS

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:17.180
WE STILL ARE TODAY, AND

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.230
ESTABLISHED MANY OF OUR

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:20.210
NATIONWIDE SERVICES.

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:24.540
SO PATTI, IF WE MOVE FORWARD TO

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:27.530
THE MODERN ERA, IS JUST THE

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:30.050
FOURTH PERSON TO SERVE AS THE

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:32.240
DIRECTOR OF THE LIBRARY SINCE IT

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.649
HAS BEEN NAMED THE NATIONAL

00:08:33.649 --> 00:08:35.579
LIBRARY OF MEDICINE.

00:08:35.579 --> 00:08:37.919
AND I HAVE HAD THE DISTINCT

00:08:37.919 --> 00:08:41.120
PLEASURE AND PRIVILEGE OF

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.559
KNOWING ALL OF THESE GREAT

00:08:42.559 --> 00:08:46.009
LEADERS AND WORKING FOR AND WITH

00:08:46.009 --> 00:08:47.350
THREE OF THEM NOW INCLUDING

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:48.970
PATTI.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:51.139
IN MY VIEW, THEY ALL REPRESENT

00:08:51.139 --> 00:08:52.930
EXACTLY THE RIGHT CHOICE AT THE

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:55.300
RIGHT TIME.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.170
IN THE CASE OF PATTI'S THREE

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:59.070
PREDECESSORS, EACH PREPARED THE

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:00.999
WAY FOR THE NEXT PERSON.

00:09:00.999 --> 00:09:03.540
IN ESSENCE, TRANSFORMING THE

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:05.860
NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE AND

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:08.620
ITS DIRECTORSHIP INTO A JOB THAT

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:11.870
WOULD APPEAL TO THE NEXT PERSON.

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.489
WE ARE ALL FORTUNATE THAT DON

00:09:14.489 --> 00:09:16.370
LIN BERG'S EXPANSION OF NLM'S

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:18.619
PROGRAM IN SCIENTIFIC DATA,

00:09:18.619 --> 00:09:20.160
ELECTRONIC HEALTH RECORD,

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.620
SERVICES TO PATIENTS AND THE

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.899
PUBLIC HAVE MADE THIS JOB

00:09:23.899 --> 00:09:26.179
APRAKTIVE TO PATTI BRENNAN.

00:09:26.179 --> 00:09:28.809
SO IT IS MY GREAT PLEASURE TO

00:09:28.809 --> 00:09:31.160
INTRODUCE PATRICIA FLATLEY

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:33.110
BRENNAN TO PRESENT HER FIRST

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:35.660
PUBLIC REMARKS AS THE DIRECTOR

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:45.230
OF THE NATIONAL LIBRARY OF

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:49.639
MEDICINE.

00:09:49.639 --> 00:09:54.050
PATTI?

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:58.459
[APPLAUSE]

00:09:58.459 --> 00:10:02.879
&gt;&gt; WOW.

00:10:02.879 --> 00:10:05.131
I FEEL VERY WELCOMED, AND I WANT

00:10:05.131 --> 00:10:06.300
TO THANK YOU ALL FOR GIVING UP

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:08.670
THIS FINALLY BEAUTIFUL AFTERNOON

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:09.670
IN WASHINGTON, D.C.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.670
TO COME

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:11.670
INSIDE.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.119
I AM DELIGHTED, HONORED AND JUST

00:10:14.119 --> 00:10:16.809
ABSOLUTELY GRATIFIED TO BE

00:10:16.809 --> 00:10:19.069
STANDING HERE AS THE FOURTH

00:10:19.069 --> 00:10:20.319
DIRECTOR OF THE NATIONAL LIBRARY

00:10:20.319 --> 00:10:22.970
OF MEDICINE IN A LINE OF 19

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:24.180
IMPORTANT LEADERS, BUT NONE HAS

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.699
BEEN MORE IMPORTANT THAN BETSY

00:10:25.699 --> 00:10:27.290
HUMPHREYS, WHO TOOK THE

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:29.269
RESPONSIBILITY FOR A 16-MONTH

00:10:29.269 --> 00:10:31.529
PERIOD TO TRANSITION, TO

00:10:31.529 --> 00:10:33.439
CONTINUE TO ACCELERATE AND TO

00:10:33.439 --> 00:10:35.549
BRING THE LIBRARY TO A PLACE

00:10:35.549 --> 00:10:37.450
THAT IT NEEDS TO BE, AND I THANK

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:42.509
HER SO MUCH FOR HER WORK.

00:10:42.509 --> 00:10:46.399
[APPLAUSE]

00:10:46.399 --> 00:10:51.290
I ALSO WANT TO THANK THE

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.899
AUDIOVISUAL PROGRAM DEVELOPMENT

00:10:53.899 --> 00:10:55.179
BRANCH AND THE COMMUNICATIONS

00:10:55.179 --> 00:10:56.600
TEAM FOR THIS TREMENDOUS

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:57.600
AFTERNOON.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:58.600
IT'S GOING TO BE A GREAT TIME.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:10:59.600
THEY WORKED VERY HARD AND THEY

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:00.600
SPENT AN AWFUL LOT OF TIME

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.290
PREPARING MATERIALS TO HELP YOU

